# Never relax the compliance check

`patient-library/src/lib/compliance.ts` is the one real implementation: **52 word-boundary rules**
in four groups — 8 superlatives, 4 outcome claims, 5 booking CTAs, 36 condition names. It encodes
the DHA advertising content standards, the MOHAP booking-CTA rule, and the no-condition-names rule.

**A build that goes green because a rule was loosened has removed the product's core legal
constraint, silently and invisibly. Fix the content, never the check.**

Import that module. Never re-implement it and never write a second blocklist — two files already
carry their own weaker `includes()` lists and all 36 condition names pass both, which is exactly
the failure mode the module's own header warns about.

## What patient-facing copy must not contain

- **No superlatives or outcome claims** — "best", "safest", "guaranteed", "cure", "eliminates".
- **No booking calls to action** — "book now", "schedule an appointment". These reclassify the site
  as medical advertisement under MOHAP.
- **No condition or diagnosis names** — sciatica, arthritis, frozen shoulder, herniated disc,
  tennis elbow, plantar fasciitis, and 30 more. Navigation is **by body area, never by condition**
  (decision D-001), and that applies to comments, identifiers, filenames and commit messages too.
- Alt text is checked as well: it is read aloud to patients, so it is patient-facing copy.

## Other locked product decisions

- **No analytics, accounts, tracking or backend** (D-007). Two `localStorage` keys are permitted —
  last chosen area and text size — and nothing else. The Vercel `webAnalytics` flag is not coming
  back; do not restore `astro.config.mjs` from git history, which still contains it.
- **17px base font. Areas sort head to toe, never alphabetically** (D-014).
- **The site describes body areas, never the patient.** It does not name a condition, suggest a
  cause, or estimate severity. Open decision D8 is whether a regulator reads this as education or
  as advertisement, and the body map is the most exposed surface on the site.

Decisions live in `anatomy-explorer/memory.md` (A-001..A-014) and `patient-library/memory.md`
(D-001..D-028). Append a new entry rather than silently reversing an old one.
